Dear Valued Customer, We hope this message finds you well. As part of our ongoing commitment to maintaining the highest security standards for our users, we have recently identified a critical vulnerability in the firmware of certain routers, including models commonly used in home networks. To protect your network and personal information, it is essential that you perform an immediate firmware upgrade. Failure to do so may expose your network to potential threats, including unauthorized access and data breaches. Please follow these simple steps to complete the upgrade: 1. Click on the link below to access the firmware upgrade portal: [http://secure-upgrade.yournetworkprovider.com](http://secure-upgrade.yournetworkprovider.com) 2. Log in using your account credentials. If you have forgotten your password, you can easily reset it via the link provided on the login page. 3. Once logged in, follow the on-screen instructions to download and install the latest firmware version. This process should take only a few minutes and will greatly enhance your device's security. Please be aware that if you do not complete this upgrade within the next 48 hours, your router may be temporarily disabled to protect our network and other users. If you encounter any issues during the upgrade process or have any questions, our dedicated support team is available 24/7 to assist you. You can reach us directly at support@yournetworkprovider.com or call